Nutrition in the sidebar has three tabs.

## Meal plans

Your meal plans, each with a line saying what it is ("Training day 2,100 kcal · rest day 1,850 ·
5 meals · Adaptive targets") and how many clients have it. A meal plan can be just targets
(calories and protein, say) or full meals: the same thing, more filled in. If you don't coach food,
you never need this page; clients log against their own targets.

A plan's targets: calories you set, or **Adaptive targets** that follow each client's own goal pace;
protein, carbs and fat (leave one empty and they keep their own); and more targets, at least, at
most or about: fibre, salt, sugar, saturated fat, and vitamins and minerals. Many foods don't list
vitamins, so a vitamin target is only as good as the labels. Tick what the plan is good for
(dairy-free, vegetarian…). Changes save as you go.

## Recipes

Your recipes are the same ones as in your own diary. Each has its ingredients for the whole recipe,
how many servings it makes, how long it takes, a method, a photo, and what it's good for; one
serving is worked out from the ingredients. The list shows where each is used in your meal plans.
Adding a recipe to a meal plan copies it, so changing the recipe later doesn't change plans
you've given.

## Rules

How targets are set: the built-in Adaptive targets (a standard formula first, then corrected from
their weight and food trend after about two weeks), with your trend window for new plans, and any
nutrition plugins you've added. Food swaps: only your swaps, or your swaps then foods close to the
plan (the same kind of food, within 15% of the calories and protein). Logging anything else is
always allowed; it shows as off plan.
